    "image_path": "images/slide_02.png",
    "page_text_ocr_zh": "给读者的话\n看了这本书，你一定会想，如果真有彩蛋，那\n该多好！妈妈可以做出有美丽图案的彩蛋饼，还可\n以做五颜六色的生日蛋糕。\n可是，为什么那位妈妈用彩蛋做出的鸡蛋饼却\n是黑糊糊的，孩子不愿吃呢？\n原来，她把红、黄、蓝、绿……几个彩蛋打在\n一个碗里，经过搅拌，就变成了黑色！\n现在你知道了，如果你的颜色盒里缺少黑色，\n你该用哪几种颜色把它调出来了吧。",
    "page_text_en": "A Message to the Reader\nAfter reading this book, you must be thinking, if there were really colored eggs, how wonderful that would be! Mom could make colorful pancakes with beautiful patterns, and also make birthday cakes in all sorts of colors.\nBut why is the pancake made by that mom with colored eggs black and unappetizing, so the child doesn't want to eat it?\nOriginally, she cracked several colored eggs—red, yellow, blue, green...—into a bowl, and after stirring, it turned black!\nNow you know: if your color box is missing black, which colors should you mix to create it?",
    "summary_zh": "本页为绘本的‘给读者的话’，解释了书中妈妈用彩蛋做鸡蛋饼却变成黑色的原因，并引导读者思考如何用多种颜色调出黑色，画面下方配有一只正在搅拌彩蛋的卡通兔子。"
  },
